# ── Existing test artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────
_tests/node_modules/
_tests/evidence/html-report/
_tests/test-results/

# ── Secrets & credentials (Helix Constitution §11.4.10 — no secrets in VCS) ──
# MCP server configs frequently embed API keys / tokens.
.mcp.json
# Environment / key-material files, at any depth.
.env
*.env
.env.*
api_keys.sh
**/api_keys.sh
secrets.sh
**/secrets.sh
*.pem
*.p12
id_rsa
id_ed25519
*_rsa
*_ed25519

# ── OpenDesign daemon logs & generated tool output (§11.4.77) ───────────────
_tools/od/*.log
_tools/od/**/*.log
_tools/od/out/
od-daemon*.log
opendesign*.log

# ── Scratchpad / transient working files ───────────────────────────────────
scratchpad/
.scratchpad/
*.tmp
*.bak

# ── Editor / OS cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# ── Generated binary evidence that must not be tracked ─────────────────────
# Root-level generated PNG/PDF proofs (scoped to root so nested, already-tracked
# evidence trees are untouched). The negation below is a belt-and-suspenders
# guard so the intentionally-tracked _tests/evidence/ tree is never ignored.
/*.png
/*.pdf
!_tests/evidence/

# Python bytecode (never track)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Ephemeral playwright/temp installs (never track)
.ptmp/
**/.ptmp/

# Wizard test-run evidence (generated by scripts/test-setup-agents-wizard.sh)
.test-evidence/

# Superpowers scratch (progress ledger)
.superpowers/

# Resilient reindex log (generated)
.lumen-reindex.log

# Generated by the wizard each run
MANUAL-STEPS.md

# Timestamped safety backups (*.bak.<timestamp>) - keep locally, never commit.
# They contain the pre-fix content, including old hardcoded paths.
*.bak.*

# ashlr genome: keep the curated, repo-grounded files in version control so the
# routing context is shared, but ignore machine-generated churn. discoveries-auto.md
# is raw {"stdout":...} tool dumps that dilute retrieval against the curated
# discoveries.md, and proposals.jsonl is an append-only session log.
.ashlrcode/genome/knowledge/discoveries-auto.md
.ashlrcode/genome/proposals.jsonl

# Playwright browser cache (CI caches this path via actions/cache; locally it
# materialises when PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH points here). Never commit it.
.pw-browsers/

# Local .git backup snapshots of submodules (multi-GB pack files). Never commit.
workshop-git-backup-*/

# ── Docs Chain (§11.4.106) runtime state and per-run evidence ──────────────
# The per-context YAML under .docs_chain/contexts/ IS tracked — it is the
# binding itself, and an untracked binding binds nothing (§11.4.215). Only the
# regenerable hash baseline and the per-run evidence pack are ignored, exactly
# as the docs_chain module's own .gitignore prescribes for a consuming project.
# Regeneration mechanism per §11.4.77: `docs_chain sync --all`.
.docs_chain/state.json
*.docs_chain.tmp
/qa-results/docs_chain/

# ── §11.4.65 Markdown exports: generated on disk, NOT versioned ────────────
# The `.html` + `.pdf` siblings Docs Chain derives from every in-scope `.md`.
# They EXIST and stay in sync — that is what §11.4.65 protections 1 and 2
# require, and scripts/verify-docs-chain.sh checks it ON DISK, not in the
# index, so ignoring them does not weaken the gate by one assertion.
#
# They are not tracked, for a MEASURED reason (2026-09-03). The content-boundary
# gate reads a text-bearing PDF via pdftotext and HTML as text, so each export
# re-presents its source's full text to the detector. Measured on this tree:
#
#     tracked-only          LEAK — 11973 match(es)
#     + the 146 exports     LEAK — 24759 match(es)      +12786, +107%
#
# Tracking them would therefore more than DOUBLE a gate that is already red by
# design and must stay readable, while disclosing nothing new — every export is
# a rendering of a `.md` that is already public. §11.4.30 forbids versioning a
# build derivative and §11.4.77 is satisfied: the regeneration mechanism is
# `docs_chain sync --all`, wired and gated.
#
# This also resolves, coherently, the pre-existing asymmetry in which the root
# `/*.pdf` rule above ignored the root PDFs while the root HTML would have been
# tracked. Reversing this decision is one commented block; the exports are
# regenerable, so nothing is lost either way.
/*.html
/docs/**/*.html
/docs/**/*.pdf
/specs/**/*.html
/specs/**/*.pdf

# Pre-ingest hardlink backups (Constitution §9: a hardlinked backup before any
# destructive op). scripts/ingest.sh rewrites TRACKED corpus files —
# curriculum/passages.jsonl among them — through a NON-ATOMIC os.WriteFile, so
# an interrupted run can truncate the source of truth, and truncated JSONL
# parses fine. The backup is therefore mandatory, not optional.
#
# IGNORED BECAUSE THE COMMIT WRAPPER RUNS `git add .`. A backup is ~120 hardlinks
# to tracked content; committing one would duplicate the corpus into history
# under a timestamped path. Keep them beside the repo for recovery, never in it.
.workshop-ingest-backup-*/
# BROADENED, AND THE NARROW FORM WAS A NEAR-MISS. The rule above is a DIRECTORY
# pattern naming one workflow ("ingest"), so it matched neither a FILE backup nor
# any other workflow's. A pre-purge backup written here as
# `.workshop-kgterm-backup-<stamp>.jsonl` would therefore have been an untracked,
# NON-IGNORED copy of the private corpus sitting in the PUBLIC umbrella — and the
# commit wrapper runs `git add .`. Caught before it happened, by checking rather
# than trusting the claim that the narrow rule covered it.
#
# Both spellings, any workflow name, file or directory.
.workshop-*-backup-*
.workshop-*-backup-*/
